# Review and pull requests

Source: SQLGlot (`CONTRIBUTING.md`).

- One well-defined change per pull request. Conventional Commits for the title.
- Behavior needs a test. API changes need a docstring update.
- A maintainer reviews the pull request. "An LLM wrote it" does not answer a review question.
- Agent-authored titles and commit messages end with the model name.
- Write the description yourself: what changed, why, and how it was tested.

Source: Acme policy. The diff must match the issue allowlist. Unrelated refactors, extra dialects, and drive-by cleanups are separate issues. Cursor rules are advisory. The scope check is the enforceable boundary.
